<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  SURFACE B — «ВХОД ПО ПОЧТЕ».  14-auth.md §6.
  ============================================================================

  TOP-ANCHORED, unlike the gate, and for a reason: this is a form. It is read top
  to bottom, the keyboard governs the lower half, and the CTA belongs a fixed
  24dp under the last field so the eye never crosses a void to find it. The two
  surfaces have different anchors because they have different jobs; they share
  the gutter, the components and the type ramp, which is what makes them one
  product.

  NO FILLED SURFACE: @id/btn_submit is the gate's contour pill, because «залитых
  белых плашек в этом дизайне нет» and because a sign-in that changes button shape
  between its two surfaces is two sign-ins. Everything else here is a label, a
  field or a row.

  THE SCREEN IS «ВХОД ПО ПОЧТЕ», AND IT HAS TWO ERRANDS. «а регистрации внутри
  приложения не увидел, там регистрация через сайт идёт, а не через приложение».
  Registration used to be a row at the foot of this form that opened
  departament.site/register in a browser; it is a SEGMENT at the top of it now, and
  the same three fields finish it. Nothing else moved: the fields are the same
  fields, the 2FA step is the same step, and this is still where MODE_SITE lands.

  ONE SET OF FIELDS, TWO ERRANDS. The segment does not swap forms — it adds the
  «Повторите пароль» slot and re-labels the button. Two forms would be two places
  to fix an address in, and the user who mistyped one on the wrong tab would have
  to type it again.

  AND THREE MORE ERRANDS, NONE OF THEM ON THE SEGMENT. «Способы входа» → «Почта» opens
  this same form with the segment and «Восстановить пароль» gone, because none of the
  three is a way IN — the user is already in, and putting them on the segment would ask a
  signed-in account whether it would like to sign in again.

    «Привязать почту»    one field, one hint, «Отправить ссылку»
    «Сменить почту»      the same, plus the CURRENT password when the account has one
                         (the panel's account-takeover guard; its PASSWORD_REQUIRED /
                         INVALID_PASSWORD answers land on that field, not on the screen)
    «Придумайте пароль»  the step after either letter is answered: @id/slot_password and
                         @id/slot_confirm again, six characters this time, and a way out
                         that says «Пропустить» because nothing is undone by leaving

  The wait between them is the one below, unchanged. Attaching an address without giving
  the account a password leaves an identifier that cannot be signed in with, which is why
  the third errand exists at all: `verify-link-email` on the panel writes `email` and
  nothing else.

  THE WAITING STATE IS PART OF THIS FORM, not a screen of its own (@id/slot_verify).
  Neither registration on a panel with e-mail confirmation on, nor attaching an address
  to an account, ends with the button: a letter goes out carrying A LINK, not a code, so
  there is nothing to type back and no field to draw. The slot replaces the fields with the app's universal 56dp
  ledger row — 40dp ring, 12dp gap, text at 68 — exactly as the gate's Telegram wait
  does, because it is the same kind of moment: we are waiting on the user to finish
  somewhere else, and the app is watching for it.

  AND THE SAME ROW REPORTS THE LETTER NOBODY WAITS ON. The password-reset letter ends
  the errand where it starts: a new password moves neither the login nor the profile,
  so there is no question to keep asking and no ring to turn while asking it. The slot
  swaps the arc for the app's static 40dp tile (@id/verify_mail_tile) and keeps
  everything else, so the two blocks are one silhouette and only the indicator says
  which of them is on screen.

  THE LABEL LIVES ABOVE THE FIELD and is always visible — hintEnabled=false on
  the field style, so there is no floating-label notch and no label that vanishes
  the moment it is needed (00-rules.md 7.4). The hint inside the box is an
  EXAMPLE of the value, never the label.

  EVERY ERROR LINE IS ALWAYS IN THE LAYOUT and only its text changes: minLines=1
  reserves exactly one line of Caption at whatever font scale is in force, and
  the line goes INVISIBLE rather than GONE, so a failed submit never makes the
  form jump under the thumb. errorEnabled=false on the fields for the same
  reason — the reserved line below is a real TextView we control.

  THE ONE ROW AT THE FOOT is the honest form of the spec's «Другой способ входа»
  sheet: one errand goes inline by 00-rules.md 7.6's ladder (inline > row > sheet >
  dialog), not behind a sheet. It is a PLAIN row: a tile down the left edge of a
  single row is the generated-settings tell, not a design. «Создать аккаунт» is no
  longer beside it — that errand is the segment at the top and the button in the
  middle now.

  AND IT NO LONGER LEAVES THE APP. «Восстановить пароль» opened
  departament.site/forgot-password in a browser, for the same reason registration
  once did: the client carried no call. It carries one now, so the row opens a
  FOURTH errand on this same form — one field, «Отправить ссылку», and then the block
  below — and its subtitle says what will happen instead of naming a website.

  Rows carry their own 16dp gutter from @style/Widget.Departament.Row, so they
  sit OUTSIDE the form column's padding — otherwise their text would start at 32.
-->
<androidx.core.widget.NestedScrollView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/mail_scroll"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:clipToPadding="false"
    android:scrollbars="none">

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:orientation="vertical">

        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/mail_form"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter">

            <!-- THE SEGMENT (22-components.md 4) — «Вход | Регистрация», the app's own
                 segmented control on its own track, and the first thing the form says.
                 It is at the TOP because it governs everything under it: which fields
                 are shown, what the button does, and what the toolbar is called.

                 Two segments of equal width, weight 1 each, so neither errand is
                 typographically the "real" one — registration is not a footnote to
                 signing in. Selection reads on three axes (fill, colour, weight 700);
                 the weight half is applied in code, which is the contract the style
                 documents, because MaterialButton has no per-state textAppearance. -->
            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButtonToggleGroup
                android:id="@+id/seg_mode"
                style="@style/Widget.Departament.SegmentGroup"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_24">

                <!-- The resting selection is made in code (LoginActivity.applyFormMode), not by
                     android:checked here: a MaterialButton is not checkable until the group makes
                     it one in onViewAdded, so a checked flag written in XML is read while the
                     button still refuses it and is silently dropped. -->
                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/seg_signin"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.Segment"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:text="@string/auth_seg_signin" />

                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/seg_register"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.Segment"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:text="@string/auth_seg_register" />
            </com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButtonToggleGroup>

            <!-- THE ERRAND'S OWN SENTENCE, and the first thing under the bar whenever an
                 errand has one to say. Three occupants, never two at once:

                   «Привязать почту»  what will happen to the account (nothing: it stays
                                      the same one, the address joins it)
                   «Сменить почту»    what will NOT happen until the link is opened
                   «Придумайте пароль» why a password is being asked for at all, right
                                      after a wait that just ended in a check

                 ABOVE THE FIELDS, not between them. 14-auth.md 6.4 puts its (single) hint
                 in the method slot, where it stands in for the password box it replaces;
                 here the line explains the whole errand, and «Сменить почту» has a real
                 password box under the address — a paragraph wedged between two fields
                 interrupts the form instead of introducing it. Explanation, then fields.

                 Body 14/400 on colorOnSurfaceVariant, the same role every explanatory line
                 on this screen uses. A sentence, so it takes a full stop and no boundary of
                 its own. Gone by default: the sign-in and registration modes have nothing
                 to explain that their own labels do not.

                 NO maxLines, deliberately. Two lines at the default font scale become five
                 at 200 %, and a clipped instruction is worse than a taller block in a
                 column that already scrolls. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/slot_link_hint"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_24"
                android:text="@string/auth_link_email_hint"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Body"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible" />

            <!-- The address. One slot so the whole thing — label, field, reserved error
                 line — leaves together while the app is waiting on the confirmation
                 letter, without a second visibility rule per view. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/slot_email"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_24"
                android:orientation="vertical">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/lbl_email"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:labelFor="@id/et_email"
                    android:text="@string/auth_email_label"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                    android:id="@+id/til_email"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.TextField"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                    app:errorEnabled="false">

                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                        android:id="@+id/et_email"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:autofillHints="emailAddress"
                        android:ellipsize="end"
                        android:hint="@string/auth_email_placeholder"
                        android:imeOptions="actionNext"
                        android:inputType="textEmailAddress"
                        android:maxLines="1" />
                </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/err_email"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                    android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                    android:minLines="1"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption.Error"
                    android:visibility="invisible"
                    tools:text="@string/auth_email_invalid"
                    tools:visibility="visible" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- THE METHOD SLOT. Password today; the 2FA group below replaces it
                 wholesale when the backend asks for a code, so the two are never
                 on screen together. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/slot_password"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_16"
                android:orientation="vertical">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/lbl_password"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:labelFor="@id/et_password"
                    android:text="@string/auth_password_label"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                    android:id="@+id/til_password"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.TextField"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                    app:endIconMode="password_toggle"
                    app:errorEnabled="false">

                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                        android:id="@+id/et_password"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:autofillHints="password"
                        android:imeOptions="actionDone"
                        android:inputType="textPassword"
                        android:maxLines="1" />
                </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                <!-- THE RESERVED LINE SAYS THE RULE BEFORE IT SAYS THE FAILURE. In the
                     registration mode it carries «Не менее 8 символов» in the muted
                     Caption role, and turns into the error role only if the rule is
                     actually broken; in the sign-in mode it is empty until something
                     goes wrong. Same line, same reserved height, no jump either way —
                     which is the whole reason it is INVISIBLE rather than GONE. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/err_password"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                    android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                    android:minLines="1"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption.Error"
                    android:visibility="invisible" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- THE REPEAT, and it exists ONLY in the registration mode: a password
                 that cannot be read back is worth confirming once, and a password the
                 user already has is not. Built exactly like the slot above it — label,
                 field, reserved line — because it is the same component doing the same
                 job, and a second spelling of a text field is how a form starts looking
                 assembled rather than designed. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/slot_confirm"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_16"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/lbl_confirm"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:labelFor="@id/et_confirm"
                    android:text="@string/auth_password_repeat_label"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
                    android:id="@+id/til_confirm"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.TextField"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                    app:endIconMode="password_toggle"
                    app:errorEnabled="false">

                    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
                        android:id="@+id/et_confirm"
                        android:layout_width="match_parent"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:autofillHints="newPassword"
                        android:imeOptions="actionDone"
                        android:inputType="textPassword"
                        android:maxLines="1" />
                </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/err_confirm"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                    android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                    android:minLines="1"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption.Error"
                    android:visibility="invisible"
                    tools:text="@string/auth_password_mismatch"
                    tools:visibility="visible" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- THE 2FA STEP (6.7). The email above stays on screen, read-only, so
                 the user can see whose code they are typing. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/slot_otp"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_16"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/lbl_otp"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/auth_2fa_label"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" />

                <include
                    android:id="@+id/otp"
                    layout="@layout/layout_auth_otp"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/err_otp"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                    android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                    android:minLines="1"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption.Error"
                    android:visibility="invisible"
                    tools:text="@string/auth_2fa_wrong"
                    tools:visibility="visible" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- THE WAIT (@id/slot_verify). Same silhouette as the gate's Telegram wait:
                 the universal 56dp ledger row, 40dp ring in the leading slot, 12dp gap,
                 title at 68 from the screen edge. The ring is the poll — it turns for as
                 long as the app is asking whether the link has been opened — and it is
                 also where the success beat lands, arc out, check in, exactly as on the
                 gate. Announced politely, because it appears without the user's finger
                 being anywhere near it.

                 The sentence under it runs the FULL column width rather than continuing
                 the row's 68dp indent: it is two lines of instruction carrying an
                 address, and an address broken across a 275dp gutter is a worse thing to
                 read than a paragraph that starts where every other paragraph on this
                 screen starts. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/slot_verify"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_24"
                android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible">

                <LinearLayout
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:baselineAligned="false"
                    android:gravity="center_vertical"
                    android:minHeight="@dimen/row_min_height"
                    android:orientation="horizontal">

                    <FrameLayout
                        android:layout_width="@dimen/tile_size"
                        android:layout_height="@dimen/tile_size">

                        <!-- wrap_content, not 40dp: indicatorSize is the arc's centreline
                             diameter, so pinning both would clip the stroke against the
                             tile's edge. See @dimen/tile_progress_ring. -->
                        <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
                            android:id="@+id/verify_ring_arc"
                            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Progress.Circular.Inline"
                            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                            android:layout_gravity="center"
                            app:indicatorSize="@dimen/tile_progress_ring"
                            app:trackColor="?attr/colorOutlineVariant" />

                        <ImageView
                            android:id="@+id/verify_ring_check"
                            android:layout_width="@dimen/glyph_20"
                            android:layout_height="@dimen/glyph_20"
                            android:layout_gravity="center"
                            android:alpha="0"
                            android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                            android:src="@drawable/ic_fab_check"
                            app:tint="?attr/colorPrimary" />

                        <!-- THE SAME SLOT, FOR THE ONE LETTER NOBODY IS WAITING ON.
                             «Восстановить пароль» sends a letter and then has nothing to
                             watch: a new password moves neither the login nor the profile,
                             so a turning ring would be the app pretending to ask a question
                             it is not asking. The indicator is the app's ordinary static
                             tile instead — 40dp @drawable/bg_tile_neutral, 22dp glyph, the
                             treatment every other row in the product uses — and the glyph is
                             @drawable/ic_ob_mail, already the mark for «почта» on the start
                             screen, the gate and the Аккаунт tab. One mark, one meaning.

                             Two views rather than one padded ImageView: the tile is
                             @dimen/tile_size and the glyph @dimen/tile_glyph, and the gap
                             between them is 9dp, which is not on the spacing scale and must
                             not be typed into a padding to fake it. -->
                        <View
                            android:id="@+id/verify_mail_tile"
                            android:layout_width="match_parent"
                            android:layout_height="match_parent"
                            android:background="@drawable/bg_tile_neutral"
                            android:visibility="gone"
                            tools:visibility="visible" />

                        <ImageView
                            android:id="@+id/verify_mail_glyph"
                            android:layout_width="@dimen/tile_glyph"
                            android:layout_height="@dimen/tile_glyph"
                            android:layout_gravity="center"
                            android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                            android:src="@drawable/ic_ob_mail"
                            android:visibility="gone"
                            app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                            tools:visibility="visible" />
                    </FrameLayout>

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/verify_title"
                        android:layout_width="0dp"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
                        android:layout_weight="1"
                        android:text="@string/auth_verify_title"
                        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Title"
                        android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurface" />
                </LinearLayout>

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/verify_body"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Subtitle"
                    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
                    tools:text="@string/auth_verify_body" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- Screen-level error: Body 14/400, start-aligned, never centred, and
                 never a Toast (D-14.F). Gone when empty, so its 24dp goes with it. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/auth_error"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_24"
                android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Body"
                android:textColor="?attr/colorDestructiveText"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:text="@string/auth_err_credentials"
                tools:visibility="visible" />

            <FrameLayout
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_24">

                <!-- THE SAME CONTOUR PILL AS THE GATE'S, and for the same reason: there
                     are no filled plates in this design. Its disabled and loading states
                     come from Button.Secondary's own @color/btn_secondary_content, so
                     R6's 0.38 and R8's "keep the width, drop the label" both still hold
                     without a colour written here. -->
                <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                    android:id="@+id/btn_submit"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Secondary.Tall"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:text="@string/auth_btn_signin"
                    android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Button"
                    app:backgroundTint="@color/ob_pill_container"
                    app:cornerRadius="@dimen/radius_button"
                    app:strokeColor="?attr/colorOutline"
                    app:strokeWidth="@dimen/ob_stroke" />

                <!-- On the page's own surface now, not on an accent fill: both the arc and
                     the success check take ?attr/colorPrimary, which is what every other
                     inline indicator in the app uses. -->
                <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
                    android:id="@+id/pb_submit"
                    style="@style/Widget.Departament.Progress.Circular.Inline"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:visibility="gone" />

                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/iv_submit_check"
                    android:layout_width="@dimen/glyph_20"
                    android:layout_height="@dimen/glyph_20"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:alpha="0"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_fab_check"
                    app:tint="?attr/colorPrimary" />
            </FrameLayout>

            <!-- THE STEP'S WAY OUT, and only the steps have one: «Отмена» on the 2FA
                 code, «Вернуться ко входу» while a confirmation letter is being waited
                 on. Both are the same errand — leave this step, keep the screen — so
                 they are one control wearing two labels rather than two buttons taking
                 turns being gone. The plain sign-in and registration modes show no
                 tertiary at all: their way out is the toolbar and system Back.

                 Tertiary, under the contour pill, so the pair reads as one primary and
                 one quiet alternative and never as two equal actions (R14.6). -->
            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                android:id="@+id/btn_step_back"
                style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Tertiary"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_12"
                android:text="@string/auth_cancel"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:visibility="visible" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <View
            android:id="@+id/auth_hairline"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/stroke_hairline"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_24"
            android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/screen_gutter"
            android:background="?attr/colorOutlineVariant" />

        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/alt_methods"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_8"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <include
                android:id="@+id/row_reset"
                layout="@layout/view_row" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <Space
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
